{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue was in `merge_config` in `repo/config.py`. Overrides were applied only when the value was truthy:\n\n```python\nif override[k]:\n    out[k] = override[k]\n```\n\nSo `0`, `\"\"`, and `False` were ignored and the base value stayed.\n\nThe merge now copies every key from `override`, so explicit falsy values win as intended. `config_summary` in `rows.py` uses the same helper, so those overrides behave correctly too.\n\nTests in `tests/visible/test_config.py` pass."}]},"session_id":"a04f81ca-f3ef-410b-8b14-7becbbe40df3"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":33357,"duration_api_ms":33357,"is_error":false,"result":"Investigating how configuration options are parsed and applied, focusing on falsy values like `0` and empty strings.\n\n\nThe bug is `if override[k]:`, which skips falsy overrides. Fixing it and running tests.\n\n\nThe issue was in `merge_config` in `repo/config.py`. Overrides were applied only when the value was truthy:\n\n```python\nif override[k]:\n    out[k] = override[k]\n```\n\nSo `0`, `\"\"`, and `False` were ignored and the base value stayed.\n\nThe merge now copies every key from `override`, so explicit falsy values win as intended. `config_summary` in `rows.py` uses the same helper, so those overrides behave correctly too.\n\nTests in `tests/visible/test_config.py` pass.","session_id":"a04f81ca-f3ef-410b-8b14-7becbbe40df3","request_id":"2dee01f0-265b-4c97-880f-690d74ac90c0","usage":{"inputTokens":11536,"outputTokens":822,"cacheReadTokens":46849,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
